## 3. TYPOGRAPHY (a priority)

### 3.1 Decision (evaluated, not just admired)
Candidates considered: **Satoshi, General Sans, Switzer** (Fontshare), with an open-licence fallback.
- All three ship under the **ITF Free Font License**: free for personal and commercial use, including apps; **no modification, no redistribution, no extraction of the font files**. Do NOT subset, convert, rename or edit the font files. For this personal sideloaded app that is fine; **re-read the licence on fontshare.com before any public distribution.**
- Satoshi: variable file with a continuous weight axis (so 600 is available), tabular figures supported (needed for timers and stats). A secondary review says it performs well at medium-to-large sizes and does not claim small-text strength.
- General Sans / Switzer: neo-grotesque, variable; tabular-figure support was NOT confirmed in my research.
- **Decision:** a two-role system with ONE swap point each — `ArOsFontDisplay` (large title, titles, numerals) and `ArOsFontText` (body, callout, footnote, caption). Both start as **Satoshi Variable**. If on-device testing shows Satoshi weak at 12–15 sp, swap only `ArOsFontText` to Switzer. Nothing else changes.

