## 6. DESIGN-SYSTEM AND COMPONENT REQUIREMENTS

Build ONE reusable foundation. Do not style screens one by one. Avoid over-engineering: build only what the inspected screens actually need.

### 6.1 Structure (single module; use the project's real root package, shown as `<root>`)
```
<root>/designsystem/
  theme/       ArOsTheme (wraps MaterialTheme), ArOsColors, ArOsTypography, ArOsSpacing, ArOsShapes, ArOsElevation, ArOsIcons
  motion/      ArOsMotion, PressIndication, ReducedMotion, ScreenTransitions
  haptics/     ArOsHaptics
  components/  (Section 6.3)
  gallery/     ArOsDesignGallery (Section 6.5)
```
- The design system imports NOTHING from feature `domain/`, `data/` or `platform/` packages. Features import the design system, never the reverse.
- Tokens are exposed through `CompositionLocal`s (e.g. `ArOsTheme.colors.contentPrimary`) and are ALSO mapped into `MaterialTheme` colour scheme / typography / shapes so that remaining Material 3 components (text fields, switches, sheets, dialogs) inherit the look.
- Provide `LocalIndication` with the press-scale indication at the theme root so every `clickable` picks up the same feedback. Material 3 1.3.0+ no longer reads `LocalRippleTheme`, so do NOT try to restyle ripples that way. Check which Material components actually honour `LocalIndication`; where one still shows a ripple, replace it with the design-system equivalent and note it in the report.

### 6.2 Tokens
- **Spacing (4 dp grid):** 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 56. Screen horizontal margin 20 dp. Section gap 28–32 dp. List row minimum height 52–56 dp. Touch target ≥ 48 dp.
- **Radii:** small 8, control 12, field 14, group/card 20, sheet-top 28, pill = full. Use `RoundedCornerShape`; do not add shape libraries.
- **Surfaces:** `base`, `raised`, `overlay` (Section 2.2). Hairline = `Dp.Hairline`.
- **Icons:** one family. If the project already depends on an icon set, keep it and use it consistently; otherwise use the smallest set that compiles. I could not confirm whether `material-icons-extended` is still actively maintained, so do not add it only for this task. Sizes 20/24 dp.
- **Motion:** `ArOsMotion` (Section 7.1).

### 6.3 Components (build only those the inspected screens need; every one has default / pressed / focused / disabled / selected / error / loading states where applicable)
`ArOsScreenScaffold` (edge-to-edge; collapsing large title) · `ArOsSectionHeader` · `ArOsGroup` + `ArOsRow` (inset-grouped list row: leading icon, title, supporting text, trailing value/chevron/toggle) · `ArOsCard` · `ArOsButton` (primary / secondary / text / destructive) · `ArOsIconButton` · `ArOsSegmentedControl` · `ArOsToggleRow` · `ArOsChip` · `ArOsStatusPill` (used for SOS readiness and module state) · `ArOsBottomBar` · `ArOsSheet` (wraps `ModalBottomSheet`) · `ArOsDialog` · `ArOsEmptyState` · `ArOsProgressRing` / `ArOsProgressBar` · `ArOsSnackbar` · `ArOsTextField` styling.
- For the large-title collapsing header, use the Material 3 collapsing app bar with its scroll behaviour, restyled with tokens, rather than hand-rolling nested-scroll logic. If it needs `@OptIn(ExperimentalMaterial3Api::class)`, that single opt-in is acceptable; list it in the report.
- Prefer Material 3 behaviour (sheets, dialogs, text fields, switches) restyled by tokens; write custom components where Material looks Android-default (buttons, rows, segmented control, bottom bar).

### 6.4 Dependencies
- Allowed: what the project already has, plus Compose libraries already in the BOM (`animation`, `foundation`, `material3`).
- **One optional addition:** Haze (latest stable on Maven Central) solely for Tier-1 glass (Section 7.5). If it does not resolve or conflicts with the project's Kotlin/Compose versions, drop Tier 1, keep Tier 0, and report it. Read Haze's current README for exact coordinates and API — do not trust remembered 1.x names.
- Nothing else. No Lottie, Coil (unless images already exist), Accompanist, Hilt, Compose-destinations, etc.

### 6.5 Design gallery (verification tool)
Add one composable destination, `ArOsDesignGallery`, shown only when the app is debuggable (`(applicationInfo.flags and ApplicationInfo.FLAG_DEBUGGABLE) != 0`; do not rely on `BuildConfig`). It shows: every token, the full type scale (with a digit-width test line for `tnum`), every component in every state, motion samples, light/dark. It is how the visual result is inspected, and it must never be reachable in a non-debuggable build. Do NOT add a second Activity.

### 6.6 Product-level UX rules (cohesion)
1. One shell: persistent bottom navigation with at most 5 destinations; **AR/OS Core is home**. Other systems are reachable from Core and from the bar. Decide the exact destinations only after Stage 0.
2. Every system's top-level screen uses `ArOsScreenScaffold`: large collapsing title, a one-line **status summary built from real data**, then grouped content, then the primary action in the standard place.
3. Core surfaces ONLY real data from existing repositories/ViewModels. A system with no data source yet shows an honest "Not set up yet" / "Coming later" state — never invented numbers.
4. Three presentation patterns, used consistently: **push** for detail, **bottom sheet** for create/edit, **alert dialog** for destructive confirmation.
5. One empty-state pattern, one error pattern, one loading pattern (loading only where real async loading exists).
6. Systems are distinguished by icon and title, not colour.
7. Do not decide exact screen layouts before Stage 0. Propose them in the inspection report using the REF-2 concept as guidance, then implement.

