## 10. SEQUENTIAL IMPLEMENTATION PLAN (the project must build after each stage)

**Stage 0 — Inspect (no code changes).** Read the Gradle files, manifest, theme, navigation, every screen, ViewModel, repository and unit test. Post an **Inspection Report**: (a) Kotlin/Compose BOM/Material 3/navigation approach/icon set/fonts/existing animations; (b) how the appearance preference is stored and applied; (c) a table: screen → composable file → ViewModel → data source → real or placeholder → planned design-system components; (d) existing hard-coded colours/dp/sp to be tokenised; (e) the protected-file list; (f) a proposed navigation structure and screen layouts (guided by REF-2, per 6.6); (g) pre-existing issues. Then continue automatically unless you hit a blocker.

**Stage 1 — Foundation.** Tokens, theme (light/dark/system preserved), type scale + font swap points, spacing/shapes/elevation, `ArOsMotion`, press indication, reduced-motion and haptics helpers, edge-to-edge setup. No screen redesign yet; the app must still look and behave the same, within the new theme.

**Stage 2 — Components + gallery.** Build the Section 6.3 components needed, then `ArOsDesignGallery`. Inspect it in the emulator in light/dark and at larger font scales; fix defects.

**Stage 3 — Shell and navigation.** Scaffold, bottom bar, transitions (Section 7.2), predictive-back check, insets. Do not change routes or destinations' behaviour.

**Stage 4 — AR/OS Core (home).** Real data only. Establish the cross-system language: status summaries, section pattern, primary action placement.

**Stage 5 — Migrate systems one at a time, lowest risk first:** Settings/Help/placeholders → Phone Activity Ledger → Routine Engine → Discipline Engine → Digital Guardian → Focus Engine → Adaptive Intelligence → **AR SOS last** (Setup, Contacts, Settings, Trigger Lab, Event Log, Help, then the countdown screen with extra caution per 4.5 and 8.2(6)). Only systems that actually exist; placeholders get the honest placeholder pattern. After EACH system: build, run existing unit tests, confirm no protected file changed (`diff` list), view in emulator (light/dark/larger font).

**Stage 6 — Polish passes.** Motion pass (everything in the 4.2 table), haptics pass (4.4 only), empty/error/confirmation states, Tier-1 glass, accessibility pass (Section 9).

**Stage 7 — Validate and report.** Build, run unit tests, produce `docs/AR_OS_DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`, `docs/AR_OS_UI_TEST_PLAN.md`, and the completion report.

